,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":131.699399007,"data":"Problem: A train departs with 100 passengers. At the first stop, 20 leave and 35 enter. How many passengers now?\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":131.699403147,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":131.699406499,"data":"[SymboLM Generation]\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":142.953534303,"data":"Okay, so I've got this problem here about passengers on a train. Let me try to figure it out step by step. \r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":142.953585708,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":152.786913329,"data":"First, the train departs with 100 passengers. That's straightforward. So, initially, there are 100 people on board. \r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":152.786981712,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":166.923041974,"data":"Now, at the first stop, some passengers get off and others get on. Specifically, 20 passengers leave, and 35 enter. I need to find out how many passengers are on the train after this stop.\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":166.923094321,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":184.028283358,"data":"Let me break it down. Starting with 100 passengers. When 20 leave, that means we subtract 20 from the current number of passengers. So, 100 minus 20 equals 80 passengers remaining after the first stop.\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":184.028362386,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":199.875183641,"data":"But then, 35 new passengers get on the train. So, we add those 35 to the current number of passengers, which is 80. Adding 35 to 80 gives us 115 passengers.\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":199.875288806,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":214.60720847,"data":"Wait, let me double-check that. Starting at 100, subtract 20, which is 80. Then add 35, which brings us to 115. That seems right. \r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":214.607250957,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":214.607256655,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":214.60726155,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":214.607266142,"data":"Extracted Answer: None\r\n"}
